Month = {JAN 1},
Abstract = {With the importance of open spaces to urban quality of life being
   increasingly recognized, knowledge about which spatial characteristics
   influence open space use, how, and why is of growing interest to open
   space researchers, designers and managers. Through an observational
   survey of Southbank Promenade in Melbourne, Australia, the research
   examines how various specific design characteristics of open spaces
   correspond to their actual uses. The findings show that different levels
   and kinds of uses are associated with the different space features of
   three distinct sections of Southbank Promenade, under varying time and
   weather conditions.},
